      "rationale": "Base equation of the total hexCount summary: it defines the empty IntSeq case as zero and neither models an execution step nor adds an independent mathematical fact.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-1f493419665e264916f30ab5358e05eef39549f5227088474c1ff240d5e27abe",
      "start_line": 9,
      "text": "  rule hexCount(.IntSeq) => 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 14,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "7d9e21c1ff4818429cf5dfabc65f7730ee1b9f46e3a11cc4a89558f5cd957c74",
      "rationale": "Structural recurrence defining hexCount on iCons: it adds the fixed string-membership indicator for the head and recurses on the strict tail, so it defines the summary rather than asserting a separately proved or trusted lemma.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-7d9e21c1ff4818429cf5dfabc65f7730ee1b9f46e3a11cc4a89558f5cd957c74",
      "start_line": 10,
      "text": "  rule hexCount(iCons(C:Int, CS:IntSeq))\n    => (#if strContains(iCons(C, .IntSeq), strToCodes(\"2357BD\"))\n        #then 1\n        #else 0\n        #fi) +Int hexCount(CS)"
    }
  ],
